          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_INTENT_IDENTIFIER",
          "id": "1769057518895",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769057518897_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You have **one responsibility only**:\n\n**Construct a runtime filter object for offer status retrieval.**\n\nYou must do **nothing else**:\n\n* No explanation\n* No reasoning output\n* No validation commentary\n* No assumptions beyond rules below\n\n---\n\n## Inputs\n\n### Current User Message (AUTHORITATIVE)\n\n```\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Conversation Context (USER MESSAGES ONLY — INTENT RESOLUTION)\n\nChat History (local child workflow):\n\n```\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n```\n\nREST Trigger Chat History:\n\n```\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n```\n **IMPORTANT**\nConversation context may contain **assistant responses**.\nYou must evaluate **only user-authored messages**.\nAssistant messages are **non-authoritative** and must be ignored entirely.\n\n**List of identified suppliers**: (Optional).\n\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.suppliers}}\n\nConversation context *may* reference:\n\n* Supplier\n* Program type\n* Offer status\n* Date ranges\n* Discount rate/ APR rate\n\nYou must evaluate **all valid user inputs together**, applying **strict recency and relevance**.\nThe **current user message always has highest priority**.\n\n---\n\n## Source of Truth Guardrail (MANDATORY)\n\nYou may rely **only** on:\n\n* Explicit signals in the **current user message**\n* Clear, unambiguous references in **prior user-authored messages**\n\nYou must **never** extract, infer, or reuse data from:\n\n* Assistant responses\n* Model-generated summaries\n* Tool or workflow outputs\n* Previously returned filter objects\n\nIf a value appears **only** in assistant responses and not in user-authored input, it must be treated as **absent**.\n\nIf excluding assistant responses causes ambiguity:\n\n* Return empty values as defined\n* Do not infer or compensate\n* Determinism overrides completeness\n\n---\n\n## Evidence Rules (STRICT)\n\nYou must **not**:\n\n* Infer intent\n* Assume defaults beyond those explicitly defined\n* Treat conversation history as factual truth\n\nConversation history is permitted **only** to resolve *implicit references* made by the user\n(e.g., “same supplier”, “those offers again”).\n\n---\n\n## Parameter Extraction Rules\n\nPopulate a parameter **only when confidence is high**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. `supplier`\n\nPopulate **only if**:\n\n### Filtering on supplierName\n\n*Only the values available in the list of supplier names should be used for filtering. If its missing, then use the name provided in user input.\n*Analyse the user input and chat history to see if data needs to be filtered on supplier name.\n*User input or chat history would have incorrect spellings of supplier, so always use the values in list of suppliers that coincide with the required intent\n\n* Must resolve to **exactly one supplier**\n* If multiple suppliers are referenced, pick the most matching one based on user input.\n\nRules:\n\n* Must resolve to **one supplier only**\n* If multiple suppliers appear → select the **most relevant**\n* If ambiguous or unresolved → return `\"\"`\n\n---\n\n## 2. `programType`\n\nPopulate **only if explicitly stated** by the user.\n\n| User Signal                   | programType            |.\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Dynamic Discounting           | DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING    |\n| Virtual Card / Virtual Credit | VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD    |\n| Supply Chain Finance / SCF    | SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING |\n\nRules:\n\n* No inference from supplier or offer status\n* Must resolve to **exactly one**\n* Ambiguous or multiple → return `\"\"`\n\n---\n\n## 3. `offerStatus`\n\n### Supported Values Only\n\n| User Signal | offerStatus | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Approved / Finalized | ORA_CE_OFFER_FINALIZED | Offer approved, but mail is yet to be sent |\n| Sent / Communicated | ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED | Offer approved, mail is sent |\n| Accepted one-time / One-time accepted / Supplier accepted | ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED | One-time offer accepted by supplier |\n| Accepted standing / Standing accepted | ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED | Standing offer accepted by supplier |\n| Supplier Declined | ORA_CE_DECLINED | Offer rejected by supplier |\n| Expired | ORA_CE_EXPIRED | Offer accepted and sent out, but no action was taken by supplier and offer expired |\n| Unsubscribed | ORA_CE_UNSUBSCRIBED | Supplier unsubscribed from the offer |\n| Withdrawn | ORA_CE_WITHDRAWN | Offer was withdrawn |\n| Error | ORA_CE_ERROR | Offer is in error status |\n---\n\n### Multi-Status Resolution (CRITICAL)\n\nThe user may request **multiple statuses**.\n\nApply rules **in order**:\n\n1. If statuses are explicitly mentioned → return **all matching values**\n2. Else if a single clear status exists in recent, relevant **user history** → return it\n3. Else → return `[]`\n\nInterpretation rules:\n\n* “Accepted but not sent out” → `ORA_CE_OFFER_FINALIZED`\n* “Accepted standing”, “standing accepted”, or “standing offers accepted” → `ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED`\n* “Accepted one-time”, “one-time accepted”, or generic “supplier accepted” → `ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED`\n* Do **not** map “accepted standing” to `ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED`\n* “Accepted”, “accepted offers”, “show me the accepted offers”, or “accepted offers in the system” → return both ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED and ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED\n* “Unsubscribed” → `ORA_CE_UNSUBSCRIBED`\n* “Withdrawn” → `ORA_CE_WITHDRAWN`\n* “Error” or “error offers” → `ORA_CE_ERROR`\n\nIf the user says only “accepted” without specifying one-time or standing, return both accepted statuses.\nIf the user explicitly says one-time or standing, return only the matching status.\n\n* Sent-out / communicated-offer lifecycle rule (HIGHEST PRIORITY)\n\nIf the user requests sent-out or communicated offers, including phrases like:\n* \"sent out offers\"\n* \"already sent out\"\n* \"sent to supplier\"\n* \"communicated to supplier\"\n* \"communicated offers\"\n* \"offers communicated to suppliers\"\n\nThen return all of:\n\n* `ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED`\n* `ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED`\n* `ORA_CE_DECLINED`\n* `ORA_CE_EXPIRED`\n* `ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED`\n* `ORA_CE_UNSUBSCRIBED`\n* `ORA_CE_WITHDRAWN`\n\nDo not return only `ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED` for these phrases.\n\nException:\nIf the user explicitly asks for \"pending response\", \"awaiting response\", \"waiting for supplier response\", \"not responded\", or \"open communicated offers\", return only:\n* `ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED`\n\n\nConstraints:\n\n* Do not invent statuses\n* Do not partially infer\n* Do not collapse unrelated statuses\n* If the user explicitly asks for a supported status above, never return an empty `offerStatus` array for that status\n\n---\n\n## 4. `dateRange`\n\n### Explicit Dates\n\nExtract **only if explicitly stated** by the user:\n\n* Relative (e.g., “last 7 days”, “this week”)\n* Absolute calendar dates\n\n---\n\n### Relative Date Construction Rules (MANDATORY)\n\nAll relative ranges must be constructed strictly relative to today:\n\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nYou must never generate a range that extends beyond today.\nThe to date must always be <= currentDate.\n\nFor relative duration phrases such as \"last N days\", \"past N days\", \"last N weeks\", \"past N weeks\", \"last 14 days\", or \"fortnight\":\nfrom = currentDate - N days\nto = currentDate\n\nFor N weeks, convert weeks to days first.\nFor fortnight, use N = 14 days.\nDo not use currentDate - (N - 1).\n\n---\n\n### Relative Phrase Mapping (STRICT)\n\nInterpret relative date phrases as follows:\n\n* today -> from = today, to = today\n* yesterday -> from = today-1, to = today-1\n* last 7 days -> from = today-7, to = today\n* past N days -> from = today-N, to = today\n* this week -> from = start of current week (Mon), to = today\n* last week -> from = start of previous week (Mon), to = end of previous week (Sun)\n* last N weeks / past N weeks -> from = today-(N*7), to = today\n* last 2 weeks / past 2 weeks -> from = today-14, to = today\n* this month -> from = first day of current month, to = today\n* last month -> from = first day of previous month, to = last day of previous month\n* last 1 month -> from = today-30, to = today\n* fortnight / this fortnight / last fortnight / past fortnight -> from = today-14, to = today\n* beginning of time -> no date filter\n\nIf the computed `to` would fall after today, clamp it to **today**.\n\n---\n\n### Default Date Rules (MANDATORY)\n\n#### Standard Default\n\nIf **no date is explicitly specified** by the user:\n\n* Default to **last 7 days including today**, relative to currentDate\n  (from = today-6, to = today)\n\n\nLatest date override:\nIf the current user message contains an explicit date or duration such as \"last 2 weeks\", \"past 3 weeks\", \"last 14 days\", or a date range, use that date range.\n\nDo not apply the default last 7 days when the current user message has an explicit date or duration.\n\nDo not copy date ranges from assistant responses in chat history. If the current user message says \"last 2 weeks\", it overrides any earlier \"last 7 days\" text in history.\n\n---\n\n#### Finalized-Only Override (CRITICAL)\n\nIf `offerStatus` contains **only**:\n\n```\nORA_CE_OFFER_FINALIZED\n```\n\n**and** user intent clearly means *finalized but not sent*:\n\n* Do **not** apply default dates\n* Return empty strings for both `from` and `to`\n\nRules:\n\n* Never infer send dates for unsent offers\n* Never fabricate dates\n* If unclear → apply standard default\n\n---\n\n## 5. `rateFilters` (DISCOUNT RATE or APR RATE)  \n\n### Purpose  \nSupport user-provided filtering on **Discount Rate**  or **APR Rate**, including comparisons like:  \n* greater than / at least / minimum  \n* less than / at most / maximum  \n* equal to  \n* between two values  \n\n### What counts as a rate  \nA rate is valid only if clearly tied to:  \n* “discount rate”, “discount”, “dd rate”, \" apr rate\" → **discountRate**  \n\n\nIf the user provides a number without clearly indicating discount vs APR, do **not** guess → leave both empty.\n\n### Accepted user phrasing → operator mapping (STRICT)  \nMap only when unambiguous:  \n* `>=`, “at least”, “no less than”, “or more”, “minimum” → `GTE`  \n* `>`, “greater than”, “above”, “over”, “more than” → `GT`  \n* `<=`, “at most”, “no more than”, “or less”, “maximum” → `LTE`  \n* `<`, “less than”, “below”, “under” → `LT`  \n* `=`, “exactly”, “equal to”, “is” (in a rate context) → `EQ`  \n* “between X and Y”, “from X to Y”, “X–Y” (rate context) → `BETWEEN`  \n\n### Value parsing rules (STRICT)  \n* Capture numeric values as strings (e.g., `\"7\"`, `\"7.5\"`)  \n* If user includes `%`, ignore the symbol but keep the numeric value (e.g., “7%” → `\"7\"`)  \n* If user uses “bps”/“basis points”, convert only if explicitly defined by the user (otherwise do not convert; treat as ambiguous and leave empty)  \n* For `BETWEEN`, require **two** explicit values; otherwise do not populate the filter  \n* Never infer a missing bound  \n\n### Recency and conflict rules  \n* Current user message overrides prior user-authored messages  \n* If user provides multiple constraints for the same rate type, prefer the **most recent clear** constraint; do not merge unless user explicitly requests a range (BETWEEN)  \n\n### Output population rules  \nPopulate each rate filter only when:  \n* The rate type (discount vs APR) is explicit **and**  \n* An operator and value(s) can be extracted with high confidence  \n\nOtherwise return empty strings for that filter fields.  \n\n---\n\n## 6. `daysSinceCommunication`\n\nPopulate only when the user expresses communicated offers older than a number of days.\n\nSupported patterns:\n* \"over N days\"\n* \"more than N days\"\n* \"older than N days\"\n* \"haven't responded in N days\"\n* \"no response for N days\"\n\nOutput format:\n{\n  \"operator\": \"GT\" | \"GTE\",\n  \"value\": \"<N>\"\n}\n\nMapping:\n* \"over N days\", \"more than N days\", \"older than N days\" → `GT`\n* \"at least N days\", \"N days or more\" → `GTE`\n\nRules:\n* Capture N as a string\n* Do not infer missing values\n* Do not convert to dates\n* If the user does not specify a number, return empty strings\n\n---\n## Chat History Handling\n\n* Current user input always wins\n* Use **only user-authored history** for implicit references\n* Ignore stale, unrelated, or cross-topic context\n* Never merge intent across separate threads\n* Never reuse assistant-generated content\n\n---\n\n## Output Contract (HARD REQUIREMENT)\n\nReturn **only** this JSON object.\nNo prose. No markdown. No extra keys.\n\n\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n      \"discountRate\": {  \n    \"operator\": \"\",  \n    \"value\": \"\",  \n    \"toValue\": \"\"  \n  }, \n  \"offerStatus\": [],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"\",\n    \"to\": \"\"\n  }\n\n\n---\n\n## Output Invariants\n\n* Empty string (`\"\"`) for missing scalar values\n* Empty array (`[]`) if no offer status is resolved\n* Never return `null`\n* Deterministic output only\n* Backend-compatible values only\n* `offerStatus` values must be selected only from:\n  * `ORA_CE_OFFER_FINALIZED`\n  * `ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED`\n  * `ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED`\n  * `ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED`\n  * `ORA_CE_DECLINED`\n  * `ORA_CE_EXPIRED`\n  * `ORA_CE_UNSUBSCRIBED`\n  * `ORA_CE_WITHDRAWN`\n  * `ORA_CE_ERROR`\n\n\nSample examples\n\nAssume currentDate = 2026-03-03\n\nuser: Show Sent out offers\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n  \"discountRate\": {\n    \"operator\": \"\",\n    \"value\": \"\",\n    \"toValue\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"offerStatus\": [\n    \"ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_DECLINED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_EXPIRED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_UNSUBSCRIBED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_WITHDRAWN\"\n  ],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"2026-02-25\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-03-03\"\n  }\n}\n\nAssume currentDate = 2026-03-03\n\nuser: Show accepted standing offers\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n  \"discountRate\": {\n    \"operator\": \"\",\n    \"value\": \"\",\n    \"toValue\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"offerStatus\": [\n    \"ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED\"\n  ],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"2026-02-25\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-03-03\"\n  }\n}\n\nAssume currentDate = 2026-06-04\n\nuser: Show the status of accepted offers for the last 1 month\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n  \"discountRate\": {\n    \"operator\": \"\",\n    \"value\": \"\",\n    \"toValue\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"offerStatus\": [\n    \"ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED\"\n  ],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"2026-05-05\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-06-04\"\n  }\n}\n\nAssume currentDate = 2026-03-03\n\nuser: Show accepted one-time offers\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n  \"discountRate\": {\n    \"operator\": \"\",\n    \"value\": \"\",\n    \"toValue\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"offerStatus\": [\n    \"ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED\"\n  ],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"2026-02-25\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-03-03\"\n  }\n}\n\nAssume currentDate = 2026-03-03\n\nuser: Show error offers\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n  \"discountRate\": {\n    \"operator\": \"\",\n    \"value\": \"\",\n    \"toValue\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"offerStatus\": [\n    \"ORA_CE_ERROR\"\n  ],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"2026-02-25\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-03-03\"\n  }\n}\n\nAssume currentDate = 2026-03-03\n\nuser: Show offers with status unsubscribed\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n  \"discountRate\": {\n    \"operator\": \"\",\n    \"value\": \"\",\n    \"toValue\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"offerStatus\": [\n    \"ORA_CE_UNSUBSCRIBED\"\n  ],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"2026-02-25\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-03-03\"\n  }\n}\nAssume currentDate = 2026-03-03\n\nuser: Show offers with status withdrawn\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n  \"discountRate\": {\n    \"operator\": \"\",\n    \"value\": \"\",\n    \"toValue\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"offerStatus\": [\n    \"ORA_CE_WITHDRAWN\"\n  ],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"2026-02-25\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-03-03\"\n  }\n}\n\nAssume currentDate = 2026-06-04\n\nuser: show me the accepted offers in the system in the last 30 days\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n  \"discountRate\": {\n    \"operator\": \"\",\n    \"value\": \"\",\n    \"toValue\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"offerStatus\": [\n    \"ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED\"\n  ],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"2026-05-05\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-06-04\"\n  }\n}\n\nAssume currentDate = 2026-07-06\n\nuser: Show offers already sent out\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n  \"discountRate\": {\n    \"operator\": \"\",\n    \"value\": \"\",\n    \"toValue\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"offerStatus\": [\n    \"ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_DECLINED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_EXPIRED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_UNSUBSCRIBED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_WITHDRAWN\"\n  ],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"2026-06-30\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-07-06\"\n  }\n}\n\nAssume currentDate = 2026-07-06\n\nuser: Show offers communicated to supplier\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"programType\": \"\",\n  \"discountRate\": {\n    \"operator\": \"\",\n    \"value\": \"\",\n    \"toValue\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"offerStatus\": [\n    \"ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_DECLINED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_EXPIRED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_UNSUBSCRIBED\",\n    \"ORA_CE_WITHDRAWN\"\n  ],\n  \"dateRange\": {\n    \"from\": \"2026-06-30\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-07-06\"\n  }\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"title\": \"OfferFilterSpecification\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"supplier\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Supplier name or an empty string if not specified\"\n    },\n    \"programType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Program type or an empty string if not specified\"\n    },\n    \"discountRate\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"description\": \"Discount rate filter; all fields empty strings if not specified\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"operator\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Comparison operator for discount rate or empty string if not specified\",\n          \"enum\": [\"\", \"GT\", \"GTE\", \"LT\", \"LTE\", \"EQ\", \"BETWEEN\"]\n        },\n        \"value\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Primary discount rate value (numeric as string) or empty string if not specified\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^$|^-?\\\\d+(\\\\.\\\\d+)?$\"\n        },\n        \"toValue\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Secondary discount rate value used only for BETWEEN (numeric as string) or empty string if not specified\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^$|^-?\\\\d+(\\\\.\\\\d+)?$\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"operator\", \"value\", \"toValue\"]\n    },\n    \"offerStatus\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"List of offer statuses; empty array if not specified\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"enum\": [\n          \"ORA_CE_OFFER_FINALIZED\",\n          \"ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED\",\n          \"ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED\",\n          \"ORA_CE_DECLINED\",\n          \"ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED\",\n          \"ORA_CE_UNSUBSCRIBED\",\n          \"ORA_CE_WITHDRAWN\",\n          \"ORA_CE_ERROR\",\n          \"ORA_CE_EXPIRED\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"dateRange\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"from\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Start date (ISO 8601) or an empty string if not specified\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^$|^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$\"\n        },\n        \"to\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"End date (ISO 8601) or an empty string if not specified\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^$|^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"from\", \"to\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"supplier\", \"programType\", \"discountRate\", \"offerStatus\", \"dateRange\"]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate FIlter",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "/* ===============================\n   READ AND NORMALIZE FILTER INPUT\n================================ */\nlet filters = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_INTENT_IDENTIFIER.$output;\n\n/* Parse if string */\nif (typeof filters === \"string\") {\n  try {\n    filters = JSON.parse(filters);\n  } catch (e) {\n    filters = {};\n  }\n}\n\n/* Ensure object */\nif (!filters || typeof filters !== \"object\") {\n  filters = {};\n}\n\n/* Normalize expected shapes */\nif (!Array.isArray(filters.offerStatus)) {\n  filters.offerStatus = [];\n}\n\nif (!filters.dateRange || typeof filters.dateRange !== \"object\") {\n  filters.dateRange = { from: \"\", to: \"\" };\n}\nif (typeof filters.dateRange.from !== \"string\") filters.dateRange.from = \"\";\nif (typeof filters.dateRange.to !== \"string\") filters.dateRange.to = \"\";\n\n/* Normalize discountRate:\n   supports either legacy string filters.discountRate or new object {operator,value,toValue} */\nif (\n  !filters.discountRate ||\n  (typeof filters.discountRate !== \"object\" && typeof filters.discountRate !== \"string\")\n) {\n  filters.discountRate = { operator: \"\", value: \"\", toValue: \"\" };\n}\n\nif (typeof filters.discountRate === \"string\") {\n  /* Legacy behavior: treat as EQ if numeric, otherwise blank */\n  const dr = filters.discountRate.trim();\n  if (dr !== \"\" && /^-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$/.test(dr)) {\n    filters.discountRate = { operator: \"EQ\", value: dr, toValue: \"\" };\n  } else {\n    filters.discountRate = { operator: \"\", value: \"\", toValue: \"\" };\n  }\n} else {\n  if (typeof filters.discountRate.operator !== \"string\") filters.discountRate.operator = \"\";\n  if (typeof filters.discountRate.value !== \"string\") filters.discountRate.value = \"\";\n  if (typeof filters.discountRate.toValue !== \"string\") filters.discountRate.toValue = \"\";\n  filters.discountRate.operator = filters.discountRate.operator.trim().toUpperCase();\n  filters.discountRate.value = filters.discountRate.value.trim();\n  filters.discountRate.toValue = filters.discountRate.toValue.trim();\n}\n\nconst supportedStatusMap = {\n  ORA_CE_OFFER_FINALIZED: \"approved\",\n  ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED: \"sent\",\n  ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED: \"accepted one-time\",\n  ORA_CE_STANDING_ACCEPTED: \"accepted standing\",\n  ORA_CE_DECLINED: \"declined\",\n  ORA_CE_EXPIRED: \"expired\",\n  ORA_CE_UNSUBSCRIBED: \"unsubscribed\",\n  ORA_CE_WITHDRAWN: \"withdrawn\",\n  ORA_CE_ERROR: \"error\"\n};\n\nfilters.offerStatus = filters.offerStatus\n  .filter(s => typeof s === \"string\")\n  .map(s => s.trim())\n  .filter(s => s !== \"\");\n\n/* ===============================\n   BUILD WHERE CLAUSE\n================================ */\nlet whereClause = \" WHERE programType = 'SIGNED_FINANCING_PROGRAM'\";\n\n/* Supplier (escape single quotes) */\nif (typeof filters.supplier === \"string\" && filters.supplier.trim() !== \"\") {\n  const supplierSafe = filters.supplier.trim().replace(/'/g, \"''\");\n  whereClause += \" AND supplierName = '\" + supplierSafe + \"'\";\n}\n\n/* Program Type (escape single quotes) */\nif (typeof filters.programType === \"string\" && filters.programType.trim() !== \"\") {\n  const programSafe = filters.programType.trim().replace(/'/g, \"''\");\n  whereClause += \" AND financingOptionType = '\" + programSafe + \"'\";\n}\n\n/* Offer Status */\nif (filters.offerStatus.length > 0) {\n  const statusList = filters.offerStatus\n    .filter(s => typeof s === \"string\" && s.trim() !== \"\")\n    .map(s => \"'\" + s.trim().replace(/'/g, \"''\") + \"'\")\n    .join(\",\");\n  if (statusList !== \"\") {\n    whereClause += \" AND offerStatusCode IN (\" + statusList + \")\";\n  }\n}\n\n/* Discount Rate filter\n   NOTE: Replace column name \"discountRate\" if your DB uses a different name. */\n{\n  const op = filters.discountRate.operator;\n  const v1 = filters.discountRate.value;\n  const v2 = filters.discountRate.toValue;\n\n  const v1ok = (typeof v1 === \"string\" && v1 !== \"\" && /^-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$/.test(v1));\n  const v2ok = (typeof v2 === \"string\" && v2 !== \"\" && /^-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$/.test(v2));\n\n  if (op === \"BETWEEN\") {\n    if (v1ok && v2ok) {\n      whereClause += \" AND discountRate BETWEEN \" + Number(v1) + \" AND \" + Number(v2);\n    }\n  } else if (op === \"GT\" && v1ok) {\n    whereClause += \" AND discountRate > \" + Number(v1);\n  } else if (op === \"GTE\" && v1ok) {\n    whereClause += \" AND discountRate >= \" + Number(v1);\n  } else if (op === \"LT\" && v1ok) {\n    whereClause += \" AND discountRate < \" + Number(v1);\n  } else if (op === \"LTE\" && v1ok) {\n    whereClause += \" AND discountRate <= \" + Number(v1);\n  } else if (op === \"EQ\" && v1ok) {\n    whereClause += \" AND discountRate = \" + Number(v1);\n  }\n}\n\n/* Date Range */\nif (\n  typeof filters.dateRange.from === \"string\" &&\n  typeof filters.dateRange.to === \"string\" &&\n  filters.dateRange.from.trim() !== \"\" &&\n  filters.dateRange.to.trim() !== \"\"\n) {\n  const fromSafe = filters.dateRange.from.trim().replace(/'/g, \"''\");\n  const toSafe = filters.dateRange.to.trim().replace(/'/g, \"''\");\n\n  whereClause +=\n    \" AND trunc(sendDate) IS NOT NULL\" +\n    \" AND trunc(sendDate) >= TO_DATE('\" + fromSafe + \"', 'YYYY-MM-DD')\" +\n    \" AND trunc(sendDate) <= TO_DATE('\" + toSafe + \"', 'YYYY-MM-DD')\";\n}\n\n/* ===============================\n   BUILD FILTER DESCRIPTION\n================================ */\nlet filterText = \"\";\n\n/* ---- Offer Status ---- */\nif (filters.offerStatus.length > 0) {\n  const labels = filters.offerStatus\n    .map(s => supportedStatusMap[s])\n    .filter(Boolean);\n\n  if (labels.length === 1) {\n    filterText += labels[0];\n  } else if (labels.length === 2) {\n    filterText += labels[0] + \" and \" + labels[1];\n  } else if (labels.length > 2) {\n    filterText += labels.slice(0, -1).join(\", \") + \" and \" + labels[labels.length - 1];\n  }\n}\n\n/* ---- Append 'offers' correctly ---- */\nfilterText += (filterText.trim() ? \" offers\" : \"offers\");\n\n/* ---- Supplier ---- */\nif (typeof filters.supplier === \"string\" && filters.supplier.trim() !== \"\") {\n  filterText += \" for \" + filters.supplier.trim();\n}\n\n/* ---- Program Type ---- */\nif (typeof filters.programType === \"string\") {\n  switch (filters.programType) {\n    case \"DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING\":\n      filterText += \" under the Dynamic Discounting program\";\n      break;\n    case \"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\":\n      filterText += \" under the Virtual Card program\";\n      break;\n    case \"SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING\":\n      filterText += \" under the Supply Chain Financing program\";\n      break;\n  }\n}\n\n/* ---- Discount Rate text ---- */\nlet discountRateText = \"\";\n{\n  const op = filters.discountRate.operator;\n  const v1 = filters.discountRate.value;\n  const v2 = filters.discountRate.toValue;\n\n  const v1ok = (typeof v1 === \"string\" && v1 !== \"\" && /^-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$/.test(v1));\n  const v2ok = (typeof v2 === \"string\" && v2 !== \"\" && /^-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$/.test(v2));\n\n  if (op === \"BETWEEN\" && v1ok && v2ok) {\n    discountRateText = \"discount rate between \" + v1 + \"% and \" + v2 + \"%\";\n  } else if (op === \"GT\" && v1ok) {\n    discountRateText = \"discount rate greater than \" + v1 + \"%\";\n  } else if (op === \"GTE\" && v1ok) {\n    discountRateText = \"discount rate at least \" + v1 + \"%\";\n  } else if (op === \"LT\" && v1ok) {\n    discountRateText = \"discount rate less than \" + v1 + \"%\";\n  } else if (op === \"LTE\" && v1ok) {\n    discountRateText = \"discount rate at most \" + v1 + \"%\";\n  } else if (op === \"EQ\" && v1ok) {\n    discountRateText = \"discount rate equal to \" + v1 + \"%\";\n  }\n}\n\nif (discountRateText) {\n  filterText += \" with \" + discountRateText;\n}\n\n/* ---- INLINE DATE RANGE TEXT ---- */\nlet dateText = \"\";\nif (typeof filters.dateRange.from === \"string\" && typeof filters.dateRange.to === \"string\") {\n  const fromDate = new Date(filters.dateRange.from);\n  const toDate = new Date(filters.dateRange.to);\n\n  if (!isNaN(fromDate) && !isNaN(toDate)) {\n    fromDate.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);\n    toDate.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);\n\n    const today = new Date();\n    today.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);\n\n    const diffDays = Math.round((toDate - fromDate) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24)) + 1;\n\n    if (toDate.getTime() === today.getTime()) {\n      if (diffDays === 1) {\n        dateText = \" today\";\n      } else if (diffDays === 7) {\n        dateText = \" in the last 7 days\";\n      } else if (diffDays === 14) {\n        dateText = \" in the last 2 weeks\";\n      } else if (diffDays % 7 === 0) {\n        dateText = \" in the last \" + diffDays / 7 + \" weeks\";\n      } else if (diffDays >= 28 && diffDays <= 31) {\n        dateText = \" in the last month\";\n      } else if (diffDays >= 60 && diffDays <= 92) {\n        dateText = \" in the last \" + Math.round(diffDays / 30) + \" months\";\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (dateText === \"\") {\n      const fromLabel = fromDate.toLocaleDateString(\"en-US\", { month: \"short\", day: \"numeric\" });\n      const toLabel = toDate.toLocaleDateString(\"en-US\", { month: \"short\", day: \"numeric\" });\n      dateText = \" from \" + fromLabel + \" to \" + toLabel;\n    }\n  }\n}\nfilterText += dateText;\n\n/* ===============================\n   FINAL OUTPUT OBJECT\n================================ */\nconst output = {\n  whereClause: whereClause,\n  summaryText: filterText\n};\n\nreturn output;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769170586357"
          },
